{color:#0747a6}Amendment denied – Contracting party must be the entity who receives the confidential mainly and must be aligned with registered vendor{color}



h3. *Term and Duration*

*Original Clause (9.1–9.3)*

{quote}"...shall expire after 10 years... confidentiality undertakings and restrictions as to use... continue to apply after end of the agreement..."{quote}

*Amended Clause*

{quote}"This agreement shall expire three (3) years from the date of termination. Each party’s obligations with respect to Confidential Information shall survive for three (3) years following termination, except where applicable law requires longer retention."{quote}

*Rationale*: Aligns with Bolt’s standard 3-year post-termination period.

{color:#0747a6}Accepted:  to 3 years Acceptable.{color}

h3. *2. Governing Law and Dispute Resolution*

*Original Clause (10.2–10.3)*

{quote}"...subject to the law of Germany / Michigan / local entity... disputes settled by ICC arbitration in Zurich or Singapore..."{quote}

*Amended Clause*

{quote}"This agreement shall be governed by the laws of South Africa, the United Kingdom, or Germany, as agreed in writing by the parties. Any disputes shall be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the competent courts of the agreed jurisdiction."{quote}

*Rationale*: Removes arbitration and aligns with Bolt’s preferred court jurisdictions.

{color:#0747a6}We propose the following as both entities are in South Africa:{color}

{color:#0747a6} {color}

{color:#0747a6}Clause 10.1 is replaced with the following: This agreement will be subject to the laws of South Africa.{color}

{color:#0747a6}Clause 10.2 is deleted in its entirety.{color}

{color:#0747a6}Clause 10.3 is replaced with the following:{color}

{color:#0747a6} {color}

{color:#0747a6}In the event of any dispute arising under or related to this agreement, the PARTIES will make a serious attempt to reach an amicable solution. The PARTIES shall be deemed not to have reached an amicable solution as soon as one PARTY informs the other of this in writing.{color}

{color:#0747a6}In this case all disputes arising out of or in connection with this Confidentiality Agreement shall be submitted for arbitration in Port Elizabeth under the Arbitration Rules of the Arbitration Foundation of South Africa.{color}



h3. *3. Indemnification*

*Original Clause (8.2)*

{quote}"...INFORMATION RECIPIENT agrees to indemnify and hold harmless INFORMATION PROVIDER from all losses, damages, costs, or expenses..."{quote}

*Amended Clause*

{quote}"INFORMATION RECIPIENT shall be responsible for direct losses resulting from a material breach of this Agreement caused by its wilful misconduct or gross negligence. No indemnification of indirect, special, or consequential damages shall apply."{quote}

*Rationale*: Limits liability to match Bolt’s lower-risk profile and recipient role.

{color:#0747a6}Rejected: No Penalties are agreed, It is important for Bolt to accepts this clause.{color}



h3. *4. Third Party Access*

*Original Clause (2.2)*

{quote}"...only permitted if (1) necessary within PURPOSE; (2) extent necessary for objectives; (3) not a competitor..."{quote}

*Amended Clause*

{quote}"Disclosure to third parties is permitted where required for internal business purposes, provided that such third parties are subject to confidentiality obligations at least as restrictive as those in this Agreement and are not known competitors."{quote}

*Rationale*: Introduces flexibility for internal use, aligns with Bolt’s operational structure.

{color:#0747a6}Rejected: The NDA already provides the required third-party-access, so there is no need for further changes as it does not provide more flexibility.{color}



h3. *5. Audit and Security Standards*

*Original Clause (2.1 + Attachment)*

{quote}"...must adhere to Information Security Standard... PUREM may audit..."{quote}

*Amended Clause*

{quote}"Each Party shall implement reasonable security measures appropriate to protect Confidential Information. No audit rights shall be granted unless mutually agreed in writing."{quote}

*Rationale*: Strips out the audit burden unless explicitly accepted._We’ve reviewed it and would like to suggest a few small edits to align with our standard terms and the nature of this engagement._

{color:#0747a6}Rejected: The acceptance of these regulations is key for Purem, therefore this document is mandatory.{color}

